# 3. FastAPI vs Flask (HOT)

| Feature | Flask | FastAPI |
|---|---|---|
| Type hints | Optional | Native |
| Validation | Manual | Automatic with Pydantic |
| Async support | Limited | First-class |
| Swagger docs | Requires extension | Built-in |
| Performance | Good | Faster |
| Learning curve | Easier | Slightly steeper |
| Best for | Small/simple apps | APIs & microservices |

## Interview Answer

### When would you choose Flask?

- Small applications
- Simple CRUD apps
- Legacy projects
- When flexibility is more important

### When would you choose FastAPI?

- High-performance APIs
- Async I/O heavy applications
- Microservices
- Teams that use Python type hints
- When automatic documentation is useful

### One-line answer

```text
Flask gives you flexibility with minimal abstraction, while FastAPI provides built-in validation, async support, and automatic API documentation, making it more suitable for modern production APIs.
```

